# Header Clock — DO NOT MODIFY

The header clock displays "Local Clock" and "Radar Site" times to the left of the alerts button in the header. Its implementation is **finalized and must not be changed** by any chat.

## Protected files and sections

- **`index.html`**: The `#headerClock` div inside `#top-right` (lines with `headerClock`, `headerClockLine`, `headerClockLabel`, `headerClockLocal`, `headerClockSite`) must not be altered, moved, or removed.
- **`index.css`**: The `.headerClock`, `.headerClock div`, `.headerClockLine`, and `.headerClockLabel` rules must not be altered or removed.
- **`app/core/header_clock.js`**: This entire file must not be modified.
- **`app/core/entry/entry.js`**: The `require('../header_clock').init()` line must not be removed.

If a task involves the header or alerts button area, leave the clock elements exactly as they are.
